# qubes-guix-substitutes: extra substitute servers for a new Guix qube
# (qubes-guix-create --unattended, --finish-install), tried before Guix's
# own. qubes-guix-config writes yours, in ~/.config/qubes-guix in dom0
# (picking from your qubes-guix-servers list); or copy this there and edit
# it, or pass another file with --substitutes FILE. While everything here
# is commented out, only Guix's own servers are used.
#
# "url URL" lines, then "key" lines with each server's signing key (as in
# its /etc/guix/signing-key.pub, on one line). For a guix-subs server, its
# own builds, then its caches of bordeaux and ci:
#
# url https://guix-subs.example.org
# url https://guix-subs.example.org/bordeaux
# url https://guix-subs.example.org/ci
# key (public-key (ecc (curve Ed25519) (q #0123...#)))
